        <mxCell id="b1note" value="One molecule, and the enzyme is still on it. The dT15 primer is annealed to the poly(A) tail, so reverse transcriptase runs from the tail toward the cap and stops at the 5&#8242; end. That is why the two or three C residues it adds with no template land at the OTHER end of the cDNA." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=8.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
